&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Service 2IC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;takealot.com&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt;, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for a highly talented Customer Service 2IC to join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us. We offer a market related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position reports to the&lt;strong&gt; Customer Services Team Leader&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day to day operations which include but are not limited to supporting and allocating workload to the Product Support team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supplying of operational reports on a daily basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Driving KPI Performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting Team Leader with ad-hoc project related tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalating IR Related Concerns to Team Leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting the Team Leaders in terms of coaching and skills development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting staff members with complex queries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pro-actively identify, address and resolve customer issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, review and propose solutions to issues identified or picked up during the course of performing day to day duties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Would be required to oversee a team of individuals when Team Leaders are absent as well as managing a team during the festive season&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver and set an example of high level of customer service&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible and Accountable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solutions orientated - able to analyze a situation and find solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about team-work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leadership skills – display the qualities of a leader and set a good example&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Committed to continuous learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Receptive to a collaborative management approach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empowering within team and structure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-centric&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully completed NQF Level 4/Matric/Grade 12&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 6-12 months Takealot.com customer service experience in related positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 6–12 months Returns experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility to work shifts - able to work rotational shifts, Public Holidays, weekends and flexible hours as required by the business operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MS Office suite - Word – basic; Excel – intermediate; and PowerPoint basic would be advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer-centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e-commerce company in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, it’s all in the execution after all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to Employ an &lt;strong&gt;Extra Ordinary Mind &lt;/strong&gt;who&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is forthright but respectful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is an expert at doing, who can not only design but also execute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is analytical, able to use data to make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is competitive, self-directed and strive to be the BEST (GREAT requires a lot of work and does not only happen during business hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is passionate about the potential of e-commerce and delivering a world-class customer experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is entrepreneurial, thrives under change and accepts it is a constant and always looks for solutions to do something better and faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is able to think about problems from a business perspective using technical and product input&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is curious and challenge the status quo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is innovative and enjoys iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is collaborative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;will be at the cutting edge of developing new concepts for takealot.com.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;thinks like an owner of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is SMART, has INTEGRITY and is HARDWORKING&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind &lt;/strong&gt;so come and join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities, to apply&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for a highly talented &lt;strong&gt;DC Industrial Engineer System &lt;/strong&gt;to join our &lt;strong&gt;Supply Chain Team&lt;/strong&gt; in &lt;strong&gt;KZN DC&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us.&amp;nbsp; We offer a market related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position reports to the &lt;strong&gt;WMS and Systems Manager&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Your responsibilities may include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Day to Day administration of Oracle WMS – user maintenance, user access, user profiles and location maintenance, level 1 support to DC operations, troubleshooting of integration issues with ERP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface between DC Operations and WMS Vendor (Oracle for issue logging and resolution. Reporting on and analysis of issue trends with WMS Vendor)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing routine audits of systems and operational processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding &amp;amp; partaking in stock sync, operating system updates, patches, and configuration changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adding, removing, or updating user account information, resetting passwords.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Answering technical queries and assisting users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting and recording of reported system problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible to align full operational flow across all departments with system processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaison with IT &amp;amp; ensuring that the network infrastructure is up and running.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist En-log team to apply all system upgrades &amp;amp; system errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quality Control (QC) support for Integration of Dimensions operational assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting in trouble shooting WCS &amp;amp; escalating to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Liaise with operational systems and service providers with management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure Quality Assurance (QA) on testing and validation,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for all technical WMS understanding &amp;amp; internal DC processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for maintenance of technical training schedules in support of operational SOP’s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for onsite WMS queries and technical support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting in arranging data in an understandable manner to assist operations with dashboards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist operations with good system practice &amp;amp; change management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzing system logs, identifying and reporting of potential issues with all operational systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Development of reporting and dashboards from WMS reporting database for OPS management teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for testing and roll-out of proposed new functionalities and bi-annual upgrades of Oracle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 3 years relevant experience within DC operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience with WMS systems such as Logfire(Oracle), Manhattan, Red Prairie, SAP, Highjump or similar -&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Information Systems, Industrial Engineering, B.Comm Logistics or similar degree preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of proficiency with MS Office packages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Full understanding of a WCS, the application, troubleshoot, problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solutions-oriented, can-do attitude; self-motivated&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, both written and spoken&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous experience in mini project management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with change and excellent team player&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with learning and adapting to new systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer- centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e- commerce company in Africa.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, its all in the execution after all.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We seek to employ an &lt;strong&gt;Extra Ordinary Mind &lt;/strong&gt;who&amp;nbsp;is Smart, has Integrity,&amp;nbsp;and is Hardworking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind &lt;/strong&gt;so come and join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot Group is an Equal Opportunity Employer. We encourage applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities, to apply&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for a highly talented &lt;strong&gt;Finance Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis) &lt;/strong&gt;to join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Cape Town&amp;nbsp; |&amp;nbsp; Team: Corporate FP&amp;amp;A, Takealot Group&amp;nbsp; |&amp;nbsp; Reports to: Head of Corporate FP&amp;amp;A&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;takealot.com, South Africa&#39;s leading e-commerce and marketplace, is looking for a highly talented Finance Analyst to own the Reporting &amp;amp; Analysis pillar of our Corporate FP&amp;amp;A team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Corporate FP&amp;amp;A is on a journey from operational reporting to strategic value creation. This role sits at the heart of that shift: you will own the Group&#39;s standardised internal reporting infrastructure and month-end process, and lead the automation agenda that frees the wider team to focus on strategic analysis, planning and CFO/CEO support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be the accountable owner of a pillar, not a contributor to it. You will set the standard for reporting accuracy and timeliness across all business units (Retail, Marketplace, Trade Optimisation, CatOps and Marketing, MrD, TFS), drive the automation of month-end and recurring reporting, and develop a Junior Finance Analyst within the pillar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pillar ownership: reporting infrastructure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the Group&#39;s standardised reporting suite across all BUs, ensuring a single, consistent version of the truth for Exco, divisional leadership and the Board pack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the design, maintenance and governance of finance Looker reporting, including dashboards relied on by Accounts Payable, FinOps and Customer &amp;amp; Insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and maintain reporting standards, data definitions and controls that safeguard the accuracy, completeness and validity of management reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Month-end &amp;amp; operational excellence&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the FP&amp;amp;A month-end process end to end: timetable, deliverables, reconciliations to the ledger and management accounts, and quality review before release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify root causes of reporting errors and late deliverables, and implement permanent fixes rather than manual workarounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document end-to-end processes, interdependencies and system touchpoints (e.g. TM1, Looker) and keep them current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation &amp;amp; process redesign&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the pillar&#39;s automation roadmap: prioritise opportunities by hours saved and risk reduced, then deliver them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and redesign processes using SQL, Looker, Excel/Gsheets(AppsScripts) and AI tools to remove manual, high-volume work from the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as Finance&#39;s lead representative on reporting and data projects, partnering with BI, IT, Tech and Product to specify requirements, get the right data points into the correct models/cubes, test outputs and sign off delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People &amp;amp; stakeholders&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise, coach and quality-review the work of the Junior Finance Analyst in the pillar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted relationships with BU finance partners and operational teams, and communicate clearly with senior stakeholders on reporting changes, issues and insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide cover and support to the Planning &amp;amp; Forecasting and Strategic Analysis &amp;amp; Insights pillars during peak cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How Success Is Measured:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Report accuracy:&lt;/strong&gt; reduction in post-release corrections and reconciling differences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Timeliness: &lt;/strong&gt;month-end and recurring reports delivered on or ahead of the agreed timetable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Automation rate:&lt;/strong&gt; share of recurring reporting and month-end tasks automated; analyst hours released to strategic work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team development&lt;/strong&gt;: growth and output quality of the Junior Finance Analyst.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes required:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owner&#39;s mindset: takes full accountability for a pillar&#39;s outcomes, not just its tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Systems thinker who understands how data flows through the business and where it breaks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional attention to detail combined with the judgement to know what matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builder and doer: designs the solution and executes it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, concise written and verbal communicator, confident with senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative partner to BI, Tech and Product; able to translate finance needs into technical requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thrives in a fast-paced, changing environment and juggles competing priorities calmly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach who raises the capability of those around them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BCom (Hons) or equivalent in Finance/Accounting; CA(SA), CIMA or CFA (completed or in progress) advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 5 years&#39; relevant experience in FP&amp;amp;A, management reporting or a finance/BI role, including ownership of a month-end or reporting process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated track record of delivering reporting automation or process redesign with measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of accounting, management accounts and financial reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced Excel and working SQL skills; experience building in Looker or a similar BI tool.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with TM1, Sage and Board beneficial; exposure to Python or AI/automation tools is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, retail, marketplace or tech highly advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supervising or mentoring junior analysts preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer-centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e-commerce company in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, it&#39;s all in the execution after all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt; so come and join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The Takealot Group is looking for a dynamic individual to join our team, based in Cape Town in the role of &lt;strong&gt;Group General Counsel.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Group General Counsel will oversee all legal and regulatory functions within the Takealot Group, ensuring that business operations, policies, and procedures comply with applicable laws. This role will involve acting as a pragmatic trusted advisor to senior management, providing strategic legal advice to mitigate risks and protect the business&#39; interests, and offering insights into the development of South Africa&#39;s regulatory environment to enhance the digital economy&#39;s potential. The role also includes leading and mentoring the legal team and developing internal compliance programs to support the company&#39;s fast-paced growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To oversee all legal and regulatory compliance functions&lt;/strong&gt; within the Takealot Group, ensuring all the business operations, policies, and procedures comply with applicable laws. The ability to drive change management and ensure buy-in throughout the Takealot Group is essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To act as a pragmatic trusted advisor to senior management &lt;/strong&gt;and to provide strategic legal advice to mitigate risks and protect interests of the Takealot Group. The ability to&amp;nbsp; understand business complexity and to simplify that complexity is essential.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To provide substantive insights&lt;/strong&gt; into the development of the South African regulatory environment to unlock the potential of the digital economy and help identify and drive stakeholder engagement. This includes working closely with external relations work streams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To lead the legal team&lt;/strong&gt; and provide necessary support and mentorship, fostering a culture of excellence and continuous improvement. This entails ensuring that the commercial, regulatory and platform compliance divisions within the legal team have processes that are agile, collaborative and responsive to the needs for the businesses. To also entail managing the legal department&#39;s budget and resources effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To oversee the development of internal compliance&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;programs&lt;/strong&gt; that support the fast-paced growth of the businesses, while ensuring shareholders are confident that appropriate governance measures are in place.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification and Experience Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;LLB degree from a recognized South African university&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Admission as an attorney in South Africa, alternatively a practicing advocate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 10 years legal experience, with at least 3 years in a senior legal role, preferably in the eCommerce or Technology sector&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-depth knowledge of South African laws and regulations relevant to eCommerce&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience in contract negotiation, litigation, and dispute resolution&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership and team management skills&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and interpersonal skills&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced and dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ethical standards and integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Knowledge and Abilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate Law (including Competition Law)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial Law&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Retail and eCommerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Dispute Resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer-centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e-commerce company in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, it&#39;s all in the execution after all.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above you are an &lt;strong&gt;Extraordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt; so come and join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Closing Date : 23 October 2026&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.takealot.com/&quot;&gt;takealot.com&lt;/a&gt;, South Africa&#39;s leading online retailer, is looking for a highly talented &lt;strong&gt;Group Head of Membership &amp;amp; Loyalty (TakealotMORE)&lt;/strong&gt; to join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us. We offer a market-related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of the role&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Group Head of TakealotMORE is responsible for defining and driving the strategic vision, growth, and operational efficiency of TakealotMORE, the subscription loyalty program for the Takealot Group. The role ensures the successful alignment of loyalty initiatives with the broader customer, marketing, and business strategies, leveraging data and insights to enhance customer experience, value delivery, and program sustainability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position reports to the Group Executive: Customer &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Vision &amp;amp; Leadership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute the TakealotMORE strategy, aligning with the Group’s customer-centric objectives to drive multi-platform adoption, retention, and revenue growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the long-term vision for TakealotMORE, incorporating innovative features, partnerships, and customer benefits to maximise loyalty and lifetime value.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program Growth &amp;amp; Development&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define initiatives to drive subscription growth, improving member retention rates, purchase frequency, and cross-platform engagement.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimise TakealotMORE benefits and offerings to ensure long-term value and attractiveness for current and potential subscribers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Marketing Leadership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the TALMORE brand &amp;amp; positioning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead brand and marketing strategies unique to TakealotMORE, working collaboratively with BU-level marketing, CRM, and customer insights teams for effective execution.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the planning, development, and execution of comprehensive, data-driven strategies and marketing campaigns across multiple channels to boost visibility, drive subscription sign-ups, enhance customer engagement, and improve retention for TakealotMORE.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Collaboration&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product and Engineering teams to enhance the user experience; drive seamless integration of loyalty features into platforms such as &lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com/&quot;&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; and Mr D.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across internal teams (e.g., Customer Analytics, Customer &amp;amp; Business Support) to leverage insights for program refinement and personalisation efforts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify, establish and manage strategic partnerships with third-party vendors and service providers to enhance the loyalty program&#39;s attractiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-functional collaboration: Collaboration with various teams such as Marketing, Operations, Customer Service, Retail, Finance, Product, and Engineering is essential. The Head of TakealotMORE needs to work closely with these teams to align strategies and achieve overall success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;P&amp;amp;L Ownership &amp;amp; Metrics Management&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the Profit &amp;amp; Loss (P&amp;amp;L) of TakealotMORE by monitoring and optimising program economics to strike a balance between customer satisfaction, value delivery, operational efficiency, profitability, and long-term sustainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor KPIs, including subscription growth rates, net promoter scores (NPS), revenue contributions, and churn reduction, to inform program improvements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation &amp;amp; Operational Effectiveness&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the evolution of the loyalty program, incorporating emerging technologies such as AI and machine learning into customer segmentation, campaign optimisation, and program enhancements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously refine operational efficiencies, focusing on seamless enrolment, faster resolution times, and automation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay up-to-date with industry best practices in the subscription loyalty sector to ensure that the strategies remain cutting-edge and competitive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth in subscription sign-up rates, retention rates, and active membership base.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduction in churn and improvement of the subscriber retention rate.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Purchase frequency and order value uplift for subscribers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Loyalty program profitability and cost per retained subscriber.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced profitability and contribution margin from the loyalty program.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Increased cross-platform usage and engagement across &lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com/&quot;&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; and Mr D.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective delivery of marketing campaigns and partnerships.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistent improvement in customer satisfaction, NPS, and program-specific metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer &amp;amp; Insights Leadership – Align loyalty strategy with customer engagement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://takealot.com&quot;&gt;Takealot.com&lt;/a&gt; and Mr D – Drive program adoption and cross-platform benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business Unit Marketing – Develop acquisition, retention, and promotional campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product &amp;amp; Technology – Enhance platform capabilities for loyalty integration and user experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Service and Experience teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer Insights &amp;amp; Experience – Leverage insights for segmentation, personalisation, and targeted engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;External Partners – Negotiate and integrate third-party loyalty benefits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualification &amp;amp; Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Marketing, or a related field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An MBA or related advanced degree is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7 - 10 years of commercial experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience presenting to senior managers and the C-suite&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in the tech sector / building a product from the ground up - advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience handling cross-functional collaboration within large matrix organisations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of P&amp;amp;L management and delivering revenue-enhancing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Competencies:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Proven ability to inspire, lead, and navigate cross-functional teams to drive results.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Thinking: &lt;/strong&gt;Strong capability to conceptualise and execute forward-looking initiatives in subscription-based loyalty management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Data-Driven Decision Making&lt;/strong&gt;: Expertise in using data analytics to interpret customer behaviour and adjust strategies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation-Oriented:&lt;/strong&gt; Demonstrated ability to initiate and implement technology-driven improvements like AI-based segmentation and personalisation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Skilled at stakeholder alignment with a solutions-focused approach to cross-departmental coordination.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, knowledge &amp;amp; abilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about Takealot Group, its brands, and customers&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker; able to build a vision for the vertical and translate this vision into product design and operational plans&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solutions-oriented executor; can-do attitude; self-motivated&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Data Analysis, manipulation, and Reporting Skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Problem-Solving Skills and Solutions-Oriented Mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical: uses data to inform decisions&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with change&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trustworthy and ethical&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced skills in the Google Suite, Slack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
